\begin_layout Standard
Solving this problem was a big problem for the Deepmind team, as it would
 require an extensive training process.
 The risk here was still relatively manageable in the form of public embarrassme
nt; for the industry, which can also be prosecuted in court for undesirable
 developments, the development of explainable policies is therefore of great
 importance.
 In the field of AI, Genetic Programming (GP) is a possibility to create
 interpretable policies.
 This is an evolutionary approach in the field of machine learning, with
 which programs can be written automatically over generations and with the
 help of selection and random changes.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Hein_Udluft_Runkler_interpretable_gp"

\end_inset

 it is shown, for example, how policies can be created for highly complex
 industrial applications.
 These are far less complex than the systems of equations of a neural network,
 but are nevertheless often difficult for humans to comprehend.
 This is often due to the fact that experts often break down problems into
 sub-problems and abstract them logically, while machine solutions often
 find only a formula consisting of few elements.
 This work therefore introduces familiarity as a measure of complexity.
 Instead of classical measures of complexity like the count of operators
 and terminals of a formula, instead the count of needed modifications of
 a heuristic, which is formulated by an expert, is chosen.
 This heuristic is improved while keeping its basic structure as good as
 possible.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This familiarity measure is calculated using the Tree Edit Distance (TED).
\end_layout

