\begin_layout Paragraph
Upper and lower bound
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If the action area has a minimum and maximum value, results outside the
 action area are interpreted as belonging strongly to the limit value.
 If the limit value corresponds to the desired result, it is assigned to
 it accordingly, otherwise the error is calculated.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
d_{bounded}\begin{cases}
0 & d(\min(\max(x_{ik},a_{\min}),a_{\max}),x_{jk})=0\\
\min(d,\text{penalty}) & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
\]

\end_inset

The aim is to find a mathematical formula that produces moderate results
 and does not produce overfitted extreme values even in special cases.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Here, a second measure, which aims to produce moderate values, was mixed
 with the main measure, which should indicate the distance to the target
 solution.
 The second measure automatically becomes the KO criterion for candidates,
 single wrong points distort the regression error beyond recognition.
 This slowed down the training process extremely, furthermore, the most
 effective solution was not a formula that only generates moderate values,
 but the use of the min and max function.
 [xxx]
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Note Comment
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
A conceivable solution would be to use a constantly increasing weighting
 function, such as tanh or log, as a distance to the edge area, to greatly
 reduce the influence of the values.
 Allerdings muss auch hier akribisch aufgepasst werden, dass die Distanzfunktion
 durch einen zu großen Zweitfaktor Zweckentfremdet wird, was zu einer kompletten
 Fehlbewertung von Kandidaten führen würde.
 Ist der Anteil der Kandidaten, die diese künstlich erzeugte Zweitbewertung
 überwinden konnten nicht groß genug, ist der genetische Selektionsprozess
 obsolet.
 Der Anteil dieser Bestrafung auf den finalen Wert wird zu einem Fehlerfaktor
 innerhalb der Regression, die ja bereits ein surrogate model ist.
\end_layout

\end_inset


